<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">International law</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">International law is the body of rules governing relations between states. Early precursors include the treaties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, which set out obligations between rulers. In the early modern period, debates about the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s conquest and the rights of indigenous peoples contributed to the work of jurists such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-vitoria">Francisco de Vitoria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-grotius">Hugo Grotius</a>.</p></div>
